      "snippet": {
        "text": "Since its debut in the autumn of 2022, ChatGPT, a generative artificial intelligence (AI, henceforth) model, has made a profound impact on our education and learning experiences. ChatGPT is an advanced language model developed by the United States-based startup OpenAI, designed to understand and generate human-like text. It can be used for a wide range of natural language processing tasks, such as answering questions, generating text, providing explanations, and engaging in text-based conversations with users (OpenAI, 2022). Due to these capabilities, ChatGPT may offer both advantages and challenges in how educators and students approach learning, similar to other chatbots discussed in Huang et al. (2022). \n\nIn the context of language teaching and learning, ChatGPT has proven advantageous for educators. Teaching practitioners can employ ChatGPT to create course materials that support language learning on a broader scale, as well as customized instruction tailored to individual needs (Cai, 2023b). For learners, chatbots like ChatGPT can serve various roles in enhancing language learning (Huang et al, 2022). As a teaching assistant, ChatGPT can offer personalized guidance tailored to individual needs, address questions, and offer feedback anytime anywhere. In the role of a peer, it can provide learners with a reference point and a platform for discussion without assuming an authoritarian role in the classroom, unlike a traditional teacher. However, ChatGPT is not without its limitations. ChatGPT may not be able to provide the desired results as instructed, and errors can even occur (Cai, 2023a). Learners may lack motivation to interact with chatbots like ChatGPT since it cannot engage in authentic human-like communication (Huang et al, 2022). \n\nSimilar to other teaching aids, when incorporating ChatGPT into the classroom, it is crucial not only to understand its advantages and disadvantages but also to assess its alignment with the learning objectives of specific classes. Additionally, it is essential to proactively investigate whether educational institutions have established any relevant policies or recommendations for the utilization of ChatGPT.",
