      "snippet": {
        "text": "While this study provides an insight into pre-service teachers' usage of large language models in mathematical contexts, it also has limitations. Firstly, this study examined a relatively small number of participants, paired with the fact that they enrolled voluntarily to participate in a seminar about chatbots in mathematics instruction. Secondly, we do not know to what extent the order in which the preservice teachers were presented with the tasks might have influenced their behavior. Therefore, the results cannot be considered representative for all pre-service teachers. Furthermore, our findings did not yield many statistically significant results, which it was not designed for either. In order to verify or falsify possible relations between behavior of the pre-service teacher, context, and large language models, further research needs to be done.",
