      "snippet": {
        "text": "New technologies, such as AI's conversational bots, can improve education. When fully exploited, these technologies will change how teaching is conducted, how learning occurs, and how the educational process is administered. The bot can help address the challenge of connecting mass-production educational systems to personalized learning environments, providing a high-quality learning experience. This can be achieved through adaptive learning scenarios. \n\nThis research seeks to understand how bots can support the teaching of students in academic institutions, such as universities, allowing them to learn at their own pace. The goal is to design and implement an AI conversational bot for efficient learning. The bot represents a stepping stone toward utilizing AI as an adaptive learning technology in teaching at academic institutions. The contributions of this study are outlined as follows: \n\n• Conceptual design of an AI-enabled bot (COFFEE) based on cutting-edge techniques and tools. In addition, the conceptual design addresses the challenge of integrating different technologies into one AI-based bot. \n\n• Implementation of the COFFEE bot using various technologies available in the market, with particular attention given to adaptive learning and suitability for students with special needs. \n\n• Development of a complete evaluation environment to test and assess the functionalities of the AI-enabled bot. \n\n• Identification of generalization and design patterns as part of the design science methodology paves the way for further research and development by other scholars.",
