        "text": "The schools included both elementary (39%) and secondary (61%) levels, ensuring a wide K-12 spectrum of educational stages. The participating teachers represent a broad range of disciplines, categorized into humanities (36%; e.g., history, citizenship, literature, and art) and sciences (31%; e.g., mathematics, biology, chemistry, and computer science), as well as interdisciplinary subjects (33%; e.g., social sciences, business management, technology and special education). \n\nThe majority of participants (91.2%) had some familiarity with AI tools in general; 85.7% of them were specifically familiar with Generative AIEd tools (e.g., ChatGPT, BARD, Canva, Tome, Gamma, Bing, etc.). Moreover, 73% reported actively using these tools in practice while 30.75% of the participants have received Generative AI training (see Table 1).",
